    "created_at": "2026-08-21T16:26:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-21T16:26:24Z",
    "body": "> I wonder what JavaScript APIs typically do\n\nWe actually just introduced this AO that deals with ranges, and it has a parameter to decide if it needs to throw or to clamp: https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-snaptointeger All of its current usages truncate, but Temporal (which has a lot of APIs that take a number from a specific range) is going to make new ones throw.\n\nWe don't have however an agreed upon behavior to follow in general.",
